    {
      "id": "ZM9nznYqHZ5NnDbXPunAH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 315.857916513257,
      "y": 45.89388712726526,
      "width": 412.1040518570122,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 867913620,
      "version": 749,
      "versionNonce": 339818156,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1780643156633,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "q = {}, level = 0\nadd 3 -> q = {3}\nadd q.top children -> q ={3,9,20}\nq.pop() -> q = {9,20}, level = 1\nadd 9 children -> q = {9,20}\npop -> {20}\nadd 20 c -> {20,15,7}\npop -> {15,7}, level = 2\nwe cant easily track level statically...\nwe need some metadata for each node\ntelling us which level it came from\nthen we just increment the level for its\nchildren\nbut what if the vector output itself is\nthe level?\nthen u check its index in the vector! that\ntells us which list it belongs to\nif parent in res[2], child in res[3] type\nthing\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "q = {}, level = 0\nadd 3 -> q = {3}\nadd q.top children -> q ={3,9,20}\nq.pop() -> q = {9,20}, level = 1\nadd 9 children -> q = {9,20}\npop -> {20}\nadd 20 c -> {20,15,7}\npop -> {15,7}, level = 2\nwe cant easily track level statically...\nwe need some metadata for each node telling us which level it came from\nthen we just increment the level for its children\nbut what if the vector output itself is the level?\nthen u check its index in the vector! that tells us which list it belongs to\nif parent in res[2], child in res[3] type thing\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
